      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (30%):</strong> Driven by N2 (IRGC incident, p=35%): an IRGC kinetic enforcement action during ongoing MCM operations triggers US military response, with the MOU framework the casualty.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (52%):</strong> Base case — N1 fails (72% probability), MOU extends without comprehensive deal beyond 17 August, Hormuz dispute persists at reduced intensity, Israeli election track proceeds independently.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (18%):</strong> N1 resolves YES (28% probability) triggers P&amp;I reinstatement and commercial traffic recovery through Hormuz &mdash; joint probability N1 &times; successful implementation &asymp; 0.28 &times; 0.65 &asymp; 18%.</p>
    </div>
